Plugin Changelog
================

0.4.1

* Settings: choosing DNS over TLS sets the upstream port to 853 (when it is
  53 or empty) and fills in the TLS name for Quad9, Cloudflare and Google
  public resolvers; going back to plain DNS puts 853 back to 53. A custom
  port is never changed.
* Validation: DNS over TLS with port 53 and plain DNS with port 853 are
  refused when saving, for the main upstream and for fallback upstreams with
  an explicit port. A configuration already saved that way (0.4) still
  starts: the relay corrects the port (53 to 853 with DNS over TLS, 853 to
  53 with plain DNS) and logs one warning per correction.

0.4

* DNS over TLS (RFC 7858) to the upstream: new Upstream protocol (plain
  DNS by default) and Upstream TLS name settings. The certificate and its
  name are always checked (system CA bundle, TLS 1.2 at least) and the relay
  never falls back to plain DNS: on failure it tries the next fallback
  upstream, then answers SERVFAIL. Persistent connections per upstream (one
  query at a time per connection, bounded pool, 30 s idle timeout). An
  answer larger than the UDP size of the client is returned truncated
  (TC=1) so that the client retries over TCP. TLS failures are logged as
  warnings, rate limited. Example: 9.9.9.9, port 853, dns.quad9.net.
* Fallback upstreams: ip, ip:port, [ipv6] and [ipv6]:port, with an optional
  #tls-name suffix; default port 53 (plain DNS) or 853 (DNS over TLS). An
  address without port (149.112.112.112) is no longer refused.
* Latency measurements: one info log line per answer that adds addresses
  (upstream and pf time), average and p95 per upstream and for pf over the
  last 256 measurements in the status and in Settings.
* Unbound forwarding: the loop check also covers port 853 and the relay
  port, whatever the upstream protocol; "Use System Nameservers" is
  detected as a "." forward.
* Catalog updates: refused new rules are shown as a warning, not an error.
* Model 0.3.0: upstream_protocol and upstream_tls_name.

0.3

* Catalog tab: search, preview and import of the lists of an embedded
  snapshot of v2fly/domain-list-community (pinned commit, sha256 checked,
  category-*, geolocation-*, tld-*, cn, private and "!" lists excluded).
  Rules tagged @ads and rules on shared platforms are unchecked by default.
  Nothing is applied before "Apply".
* Catalog updates: imported applications keep their catalog references and
  show the rules added to or removed from the catalog, to review and accept.
* Shared platform guard (CDN, cloud, hosting): a domain: rule on a whole
  shared platform, on one of its parents or on a top-level domain alone is
  refused by the model and by the relay; extra names can be configured.
* keyword: and regexp: are discovery rules: kept, never applied by the
  relay, with a single debug log line instead of a warning on each reload.
* Automatic Unbound forwarding (opt-in): one forward zone per application
  domain to the relay, with forward-first, in
  /usr/local/etc/unbound.opnsense.d/appalias.conf. While the relay is down,
  these domains fall back to direct recursion (plain DNS, port 53),
  bypassing DNS over TLS and the "." Query Forwarding; with outgoing port 53
  blocked they fail until the relay is back. Apply restarts Unbound
  only when the list of forwarded domains changes. Names already configured
  in Unbound (Query Forwarding, DNS over TLS, domain overrides), their
  sub-domains, local names and children of a forwarded parent are skipped
  and listed in Settings; no zone is written when the relay upstream is the
  firewall itself (loop). Other queries keep their path (DNS over TLS).
* Model 0.2.0: hidden catalog fields per application, Origin field removed
  from the application dialog.
* Source texts in English (translations are handled by the OPNsense
  translation project).

0.2

* Install migration fix: upstream_address is no longer required by the
  model (check moved to the validation, required only when the service is
  enabled).
* New Log page (Services > AppAlias > Log File).
* Reconfigure: the result of each configd call is checked (template,
  export, synchronization, start, reload).
* Status: widget captions (Restart, Start, Stop).
* Alias synchronization and re-creation of missing aliases under the
  config.xml lock.
* System boot: no more double start of the daemon, the bootup event exports
  the configuration and reloads the daemon if it is already running.
* Grid error tooltip escaped (jQuery construction); the grid is no longer
  reloaded twice when the page loads.
* sessionClose() removed from ServiceController (not needed with the 26.7
  core, the session is released at construction).

0.1

* First version (MVP): DNS relay, domain:/full: rules, manual CIDRs.
